mbinations starting with V followed by letters from {C,D,G,M,M}, making sure to avoid forbidden letter triples like VAA, VAD, VCN, VGC, VMN, and others, trying sequences like \"VMM\" to see if they're permitted.\n\nI land on V-M-M-D-G-C: checking each triple (VMM, MMD, MDG, DGC) against the forbidden list, and all of them pass. This uses exactly the rack letters M, M, D, G, C with M in position b as required.\n\nNow I'm scoring the word: V(1) + M(2) + M(2×4 bonus)=8 + D(2) + G(1) + C(1), totaling 15 points. I'm double-checking the bonus cell's coordinate sum confirms the x4 multiplier applies, then verifying the newly placed cells don't accidentally touch any existing neighbors on other axes — they come up empty, so the placement is clean.\n\nThat confirms it.\n\n",
